cuems-utils (0.1.0rc16) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  NOT YET BUILT. This entry is written ahead of the build so the packaging
  record stops trailing the source by two release candidates, as it did
  between rc14 and here. rc16 is the version the coordinated ecosystem merge
  deploys; it is tagged xml-refactor-merge-candidate and nothing in the CUEMS
  stack releases alone.

  * Packaging: debian/ now lives on the working branch instead of on
    debian/bookworm. The branch is kept and tagged packaging-rc14; nothing
    new lands on it. This removes the merge-main-in step that let packaging
    fall seven weeks behind the source.
  * Schema renames, none of which invalidate a document on disk:
    outputs.xsd becomes hardware_outputs.xsd, with its root element
    (CuemsHardwareOutputs), its type (HardwareOutputsType) and its schema key
    renamed with it. This resolves an audit finding where two schemas declared
    OutputsType in the same namespace with different content.
    project_mappings.xsd's NodeType becomes NodeMappingType, leaving
    network_map.xsd's NodeType as the only declaration of that name; type
    names are schema-internal, so no document changes.
  * Schema field removals, each with a registered conversion so documents in
    the field still load:
    settings.xsd drops audioplayer/audio_cards and dmxplayer/universes --
    counts restating another document's content, read by nothing anywhere in
    the ecosystem. settings documents move to doc_version 2.
    hardware_outputs.xsd drops default_video_output and default_audio_output
    -- authored choices already declared in project_mappings. That schema
    moves to doc_version 2. Verified against a real production settings.xml.
  * The generated reference settings document is corrected against the two
    audited production machines. All four player sections previously named
    /usr/bin/cuems-player, a binary that has never existed and is absent from
    both machines; they now name cuems-videocomposer, cuems-audioplayer,
    jack-volume and cuems-dmxplayer respectively. editor_url becomes
    formitgo.local, the brand hostname operators actually use. The generator
    also emits the optional knobs (osc_port, output_latency_ms) that it
    filtered out before.
  * An empty <node_list/> now raises ValueError rather than TypeError, so the
    failure names the document instead of the machinery.
  * An atomic save no longer discards the target file's mode.
  * Still ships nothing under /etc. The six XSD files remain inside the venv
    only, and no default XML document is installed -- so a fresh node still
    cannot start unaided. That is the next feature's whole subject; see
    specs/planning/etc-cuems-first-install.md.

 -- Adrià Masip <adria.back@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:41:49 +0200

cuems-utils (0.1.0rc15) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  NOT BUILT AS A PACKAGE. Recorded retrospectively: the source moved from
  rc14 to rc16 while debian/ sat on a branch nobody merged into, so this
  version never got an entry. It is written now so the changelog is a
  continuous record rather than one with a hole in it.

  * New entry point: cuems-convert-documents, an offline batch upgrade for
    XML documents, installed into the shared venv alongside the library. It
    backs up each document before rewriting and treats a backup failure as
    fatal for that document alone.
  * Reading became strict. Every document load now runs structural and
    semantic validation: a valid document loads, a version-old one converts
    IN MEMORY with the file on disk untouched, a repairable violation loads
    with the field repaired to its declared default, an unrepairable one
    raises, and a document newer than the library raises distinguishably.
    Operators get a report naming every repair rather than a silent
    substitution.
  * Documents carry a doc_version marker, per schema, with a conversion
    registered for every version step. Absent means version 1, so nothing on
    disk is invalidated by its introduction.
  * network_map.xsd: <node_type>, free text carrying NodeType.master /
    NodeType.slave, becomes <node_role>, typed controller/node/firstrun.
    DEPLOYED MAPS MUST BE CONVERTED -- both audited production machines were
    still carrying the old vocabulary at the time of writing.
  * The library gained its first write path for network_map.xml, and the
    node object model moved in from cuems-nodeconf.
  * One public API across the library: load/save/validate/from_json/to_json/
    to_wire on the script object, configuration accessors answering with
    objects, and cuemsutils.errors as the one public error module. Six
    retired entry points still resolve and warn; they are REMOVED IN v0.1.1,
    which is why every consumer pins << 0.1.1~.
  * DmxUniverse no longer silently stores unconverted channel data when a
    per-entry conversion fails; it raises DmxChannelDecodeError naming the
    universe and the failing entry.
  * Media duration is typed as a timecode, and the unused fade-profile
    surface is deleted.

 -- Adrià Masip <adria.back@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:41:49 +0200

cuems-utils (0.1.0rc14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * HubServices: stop the receive/send loops for good when the socket
    reports Closed, instead of looping straight back into another
    arecv_msg()/asend(). pynng registers an atexit hook calling
    nng_fini(), which frees NNG's global state, and CPython does not
    join daemon threads before running atexit hooks — so the comms
    thread was still polling the bus and aborted the process with
    "panic: pthread_mutex_lock: Invalid argument" (nni_aio_begin <-
    nng_recv_aio). Both loops also bail out at the top once _closing is
    set. Paired with the engine-side stop+join of the comms thread
    (cuems-engine rc_1 a4e5e61), which covers the second failure mode
    where the interpreter's GC finalises an abandoned arecv_msg()
    coroutine. Measured on the test2 node engine: 5/5 instrumented
    restarts core-dumped before, 0/10 after. ClickUp 869ed00ya.
  * cues: add VideoCue.opacity and fix the AudioCue.master_vol default
    (was 0.1.0rc13, never released as a package).

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 12:30:00 +0200

cuems-utils (0.1.0rc12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * log.py: record each message once in the journal, with its real
    priority. (1) Root logger seeded with a NullHandler so third-party
    import-time logging (pyossia via cuemsengine.osc) cannot arm an
    implicit basicConfig stderr handler that re-emitted every record in
    BASIC_FORMAT. (2) Under systemd (JOURNAL_STREAM) only the
    SysLogHandler is attached: stdout and /dev/log both land in
    journald, and only the syslog copy carries a true per-record
    priority (systemd stamps all stdout PRIORITY=6), so cuems-logs -l/-e
    can finally filter. (3) SysLogHandler.ident set from argv[0] so
    journald records a full SYSLOG_IDENTIFIER instead of the kernel-
    truncated _COMM (controller-engi). Verified on the test2 controller:
    3 copies -> 1, priorities 7/4/3, 552 tests unchanged.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 19:58:05 +0200

cuems-utils (0.1.0rc11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * parsers: stop type-coercing free-text fields (ClickUp 869cqbpxa).
    CuemsParser.str_to_value() ran every scalar through int -> float ->
    strtobool -> Uuid regardless of its key, so free text was silently
    rewritten on save. Since strtobool accepts the truth abbreviations, a cue
    named n/N/f/F was persisted as False, y/Y/t/T as True and any bare digit
    as an int -- 18 of the 62 alphanumeric single characters, plus the words
    yes/no/true/false/on/off. Reported as "can't name a cue with a single
    letter": there was never a length rule (NameStringType has always been
    minLength=1 and the frontend has no validator), the failing characters
    were exactly strtobool's vocabulary.
    Separately, a cue named lowercase none/null hit the ['none','null','']
    -> None branch, serialised to <name/> and failed NameStringType's
    minLength=1 -- a hard XMLSchemaValidationError at save rather than silent
    corruption. The new short-circuit precedes that branch, fixing both.
    Adds STRING_TYPED_KEYS plus an optional key argument to str_to_value,
    threaded through all four call sites; keeping key optional leaves
    existing single-argument callers unaffected. 'id' is deliberately
    excluded -- the Uuid() branch is the only thing producing Uuid objects on
    parse. Reachable keys are name, description and file_name; output_name,
    parameter_name, icon and color are defensive entries only.
    Full suite green (551 passed; the one failure is a pre-existing realtime
    jitter check unrelated to this change, which passes in CI).
    Verified end-to-end on test2 through the live cuems-editor WebSocket:
    12/12 names round-trip verbatim, including none/null which previously
    errored. Ships the same source as main/rc_1 @ 0.1.0rc11.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Tue, 28 Jul 2026 15:05:00 +0200

cuems-utils (0.1.0rc10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * deps: bump lxml 5.3.0 -> 6.1.0 to clear CVE-2026-41066 (high) -- XXE via
    iterparse()/ETCompatXMLParser() with resolve_entities=True default (fixed:
    default is now 'internal'). cuems-utils only uses lxml.etree.Element +
    register_namespace (never the parser entry points), so it was never
    actually reachable, but bumped to clear the advisory and future-proof.
    Full test suite verified green before (5.3.0) and after (6.1.0): 312
    passed, XML round-trips included. Ships the same source as main/rc_1 @
    0.1.0rc10 (media-duration + node-identity + gradient_osc_port).

